<title>USA: Hawaii $150 million GO bonds repriced.</title>
<headline>Hawaii $150 million GO bonds repriced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Wednesday it repriced a $150 million Hawaii general obligation bonds of 1996, Series CM issue, raising yields in the 2000 thru 2005 maturities.</p>
<p>State of Hawaii</p>
<p>RE: $150,000,000*</p>
<p>General Obligation Bonds</p>
<p>of 1996, Series CM</p>
<p>We have received the verbal award.</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA	FGIC INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 12/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 06/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>12/01/1999		8,335M    5.00  %	  4.20</p>
<p>12/01/2000		8,335M    5.00  %	  4.375</p>
<p>12/01/2001		8,335M    5.00  %	  4.50</p>
